# Week 1 — Task 2 — Phase B: Homelab Setup

## Objective
Build a foundation for cloud security experiments using separate public and private subnets and baseline monitoring.

## Actions taken
- Created `HomelabVPC` with one public subnet and one private subnet.
- Configured internet gateway routing for the public subnet; the private subnet has no direct internet route.
- Reused the CloudTrail trail created in Task 1.
- Added the AWS Config managed rule `s3-bucket-public-read-prohibited` for S3 buckets.
- Attempted to activate GuardDuty, but it was unavailable in this account.

## Verification and troubleshooting
I checked the VPC, subnets, route tables, and AWS Config rule in the console. In PowerShell, `aws sts get-caller-identity` confirmed that the CLI used `temp-user`. The `aws cloudtrail describe-trails` command returned `AccessDeniedException` because this user lacked `cloudtrail:DescribeTrails` permission. I did not count that CLI check as successful.

## Key observations
The VPC provides a recorded public and private subnet layout for later lab work. CloudTrail was already configured before this phase, so I did not create a duplicate trail. GuardDuty remains an incomplete checklist item.

